    "lawCode": "Amd §96-d, Bank L",
    "lawSection": "Banking Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4583\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the banking law, in relation to authorizing certain\nbanking organizations to establish multiple branches in an existing\nbanking development district\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThis is an amendment to Chapter 11 of the Laws of 2009 that provide\nfor the establishment of multiple branches in an existing banking\ndevelopment district by a bank, trust company .or national bank.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill amends § 96-d to make technical corrections.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe 2008 chapter had technical flaws that needed to be corrected.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2009: A. 259 02104/09 Passed Assembly/S.1936 Passed Senate; 2007-2008:\nA.1680 02106/08 Passed Assembly Delivered to Senate - Referred to\nBanks\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS :\n\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
